{
  "id": "v3-weekly-schedule",
  "repoId": "owned-v3-weekly-schedule",
  "split": "development",
  "title": "Overnight availability and maintenance blackouts leave incorrect booking windows",
  "description": "A booking preview normalizes weekly resource availability and subtracts scheduled maintenance. The current implementation drops the morning portion of overnight slots, leaves adjacent intervals fragmented, and loses a valid interval when a blackout splits a larger slot. Repair the normalization and subtraction pipeline.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R01",
      "text": "Windows use day 0..6 and minute boundaries 0..1440. Treat intervals as [start,end). If end<start, split across midnight onto (day+1) modulo7; equal endpoints mean an empty interval. Apply the same expansion to availability and blackouts."
    },
    {
      "id": "R02",
      "text": "For each exact resource and weekday, merge overlapping or adjacent availability windows, and merge blackouts before subtraction. Resources and days must remain independent."
    },
    {
      "id": "R03",
      "text": "Subtract every blackout from availability, preserving both sides when one blackout splits a slot. Touching endpoints do not overlap. Return nonempty windows sorted by resource ascending, day ascending, then start ascending, with exactly resource,day,start,end."
    },
    {
      "id": "R04",
      "text": "Slots and blackouts must be lists of objects with exactly resource,day,start,end. Resource is a nonempty string; day is a plain integer0..6; start/end are plain integers0..1440. Invalid input raises ValueError, including invalid blackouts when no slots exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "R05",
      "text": "Do not mutate slots, blackouts, or nested window objects. Duplicate windows are harmless and must not produce duplicate output."
    }
  ],
  "files": {
    "weekly_schedule.py": "\"\"\"Original PatchProof maintenance fixture. SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0.\"\"\"\n\ndef _validate(windows):\n    if type(windows) is not list:\n        raise ValueError(\"windows must be a list\")\n    for window in windows:\n        if type(window) is not dict or set(window) != {\"resource\", \"day\", \"start\", \"end\"}:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid window fields\")\n        if type(window[\"resource\"]) is not str or not window[\"resource\"]:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid resource\")\n        if type(window[\"day\"]) is not int or not 0 <= window[\"day\"] <= 6:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid weekday\")\n        for key in (\"start\", \"end\"):\n            if type(window[key]) is not int or not 0 <= window[key] <= 1440:\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid minute boundary\")\n\n\ndef _expand(windows):\n    grouped = {}\n    for window in windows:\n        day, start, end = window[\"day\"], window[\"start\"], window[\"end\"]\n        if start == end:\n            continue\n        pieces = [(day, start, end)] if start < end else [\n            (day, start, 1440)]\n        for piece_day, left, right in pieces:\n            if left < right:\n                grouped.setdefault((window[\"resource\"], piece_day), []).append((left, right))\n    return grouped\n\n\ndef _merge(intervals):\n    merged = []\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals):\n        if merged and start < merged[-1][1]:\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    return merged\n\n\ndef _subtract(intervals, blocked):\n    result = intervals\n    for block_start, block_end in blocked:\n        remaining = []\n        for start, end in result:\n            if block_end <= start or block_start >= end:\n                remaining.append([start, end])\n                continue\n            if start < block_start:\n                remaining.append([start, block_start])\n            elif block_end < end:\n                remaining.append([block_end, end])\n        result = remaining\n    return result\n\n\ndef available_windows(slots, blackouts):\n    \"\"\"Normalize recurring weekly availability and remove maintenance windows.\"\"\"\n    _validate(slots)\n    _validate(blackouts)\n    available = _expand(slots)\n    unavailable = _expand(blackouts)\n    result = []\n    for resource, day in sorted(available):\n        periods = _merge(available[(resource, day)])\n        blocks = _merge(unavailable.get((resource, day), []))\n        for start, end in _subtract(periods, blocks):\n            result.append({\"resource\": resource, \"day\": day, \"start\": start, \"end\": end})\n    return result\n"
  },
